text='''# Focused related-work review
Eleven primary academic works were checked at the stated retrieval depth, plus one provenance standard. This count includes technical reports/workshop manuscripts and an author abstract; it is not eleven newly read peer-reviewed full papers. P01's author-linked PDF and institution metadata support the reused base algorithm. P10's primary indexed extracts support fixed furniture/subspace constraints; direct PDF retrieval failed. No full-paper inspection is invented. Matrix cells provide exact evidence levels, citations and limitations.

Dynamic optimization and minimal-change repair already cover changed objectives/constraints, previous-solution reuse and stable assignments (P02–P05). Dependency propagation and reevaluation consistency are established (P06). Role-qualified decisions, conditions and ongoing authorization are established (P07–P08). Runtime enforcement provides a clear precedent for checking critical properties before accepting system output (P09). Mixed-initiative layout with fixed items and human control is directly established (P10–P11). Provenance representation is a standard mechanism (S01). None of these generic operations is a defensible standalone EAG invention.

The closest challenge is not one paper that duplicates every software field. It is a competent composition of standard current-evidence checks, permissions, changed-input bookkeeping, actual reduced-variable repair and full independent revalidation. B4 implements that operational comparison. A claim of novelty for the integration itself still needs a precise scientific distinction and independent evidence; a fresh name or different JSON schema is insufficient.

The scoped event question is whether reviewed, source/version-qualified physical geometry plus client/planner function obligations can govern reuse/repair/refusal without silently accepting incomplete or unauthorized recommendations. Correctness on synthetic controlled cases is a useful application result, not proof that no previous event system implements equivalent internal logic. Existing Cvent and Prismm capabilities overlap with the application: scaled diagramming, automated layout/seating assistance, digital twins and collaboration. Proprietary optimizer/approval/certificate internals remain unknown from public pages; neither absence nor superiority is inferred. Vendors were not benchmarked.

Primary references are linked below. Publication/inspection details are authoritative in the CSV; the review does not transfer another paper's formal guarantees to this heuristic research prototype.
'''
